+Instead of a target path, you can pass a map of options:
+
+targetPath
+: (`string`) The target path of the copy. Defaults to the target path of the given resource.
+
+importContext
+: (`slice` or `resource`) Resources used to resolve imports when the copy is transformed by [`css.Build`], [`js.Build`], [`js.Batch`], [`css.Sass`], [`css.PostCSS`] (with `inlineImports` enabled) and [`css.TailwindCSS`]. This can be a resource, a page (its page resources are used), the result of a `Mount` on a slice of resources, or a slice of these. The first match wins, and the import context takes precedence over the files in the `assets` directory. Imports not found in the import context are resolved as usual. See the [import context] in `js.Batch` for more information.
